{'symbol': 'INTC', 'date': '2023-02-01 12:00:00', 'title': 'INTEL AND UC SAN DIEGO JOIN DARPA PROGRAM TO PREVENT EXPLOITATION OF COMPUTING SYSTEMS', 'text': "SANTA CLARA, CALIF.--( BUSINESS WIRE )--WHAT'S NEW: INTEL AND THE UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA, SAN DIEGO (UC SAN DIEGO) ANNOUNCED TODAY THAT THEY HAVE BEEN SELECTED TO JOIN THE HARDENING DEVELOPMENT TOOLCHAINS AGAINST EMERGENT EXECUTION ENGINES (HARDEN) PROGRAM TEAM FOR THE DEFENSE ADVANCED RESEARCH PROJECTS AGENCY (DARPA). ADVERSARIES HAVE CRAFTED INCREASINGLY COMPLEX CYBERATTACKS IN REACTION TO DECADES OF PLATFORM HARDENING EFFORTS AND INCREASING IT SECURITY MEASURES THAT REDUCE VULNERABILITIES. ATTEMPTS TO MITIGATE THESE THREATS HAVE FALLEN SHORT, CREATING AN INCREASED RISK OF INTRUSION INTO CURRENT AND LEGACY CODE."}